      "writtenOn": "2018-08-15T01:20:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this proposed change is mostly correct. If a Get_Source_Cap message is received while in the SRC_READY state, then the state should transition to SRC_Send_Capabilities state. From section 8.3.3.2.6:\n\nThe Policy Engine shall transition to the PE_SRC_Send_Capabilities state when:\n The Device Policy Manager indicates that Source Capabilities have changed or\n A Get_Source_Cap Message is received.\n\nI\u0027m not sure if it should be transitioning to the \"misspelled\" SRC_NEGOCIATE state though as the SRC_CAP message would only be sent one time. In the PE_SRC_Send_Capabilities state, I think SRC_CAP messages should be sent until a GoodCRC message is received. So maybe this case should transition to PD_STATE_SRC_DISCOVERY instead of PD_STATE_SRC_NEGOCIATE",
